  "labelNotes": "Supply: VDD33 3.0/3.3/3.6 V from Recommended Operating Conditions (Table 6-2). 'Power supply voltage' is printed in both Table 6-1 and 6-2, so citations span two cells to stay unique. IVDD 'Current delivered by external power supply' 0.5 A (MIN) is a requirement on the external supply, not a current drawn by the part, so it is excluded. Supply currents are the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE active-mode current tables (Tables 6-4, 6-5), unit mA from the 'Peak (mA)' header; the column is 'Peak', which I mapped to MAX (judgement call; these are measured peaks at 3.3 V, 25 C). The 3.3 V / 25 C measurement statement is a section-wide default and RF conditions are not allowed keys, so these carry no conditions. Leakage: IIH and IIL both print 50 nA MAX with no conditions, one distinct tuple, so one label (citing IIH). Abs max: VDD33 3.6 V. Pull-up: RPU 45 kohm TYP; RPD excluded."
}